# Calendar System Refactor Plan
## Structural Identity Conversion (Constraint-Driven Writes)

---

## 🎯 Goal

Convert the calendar system from:

```text
string-address-based identity (chronology_address)
```

to:

```text
structural identity:
projection_entity_id + parent_event_id + layer_id + sequence_index
```

and enforce:

```text
All writes must be constraint-driven and idempotent.
```

---

## 🧠 Core Principles

### 1. Single Source of Truth

```text
Structure = parent_event_id
Order = sequence_index
Identity = projection + parent + layer + sequence_index
```

---

### 2. chronology_address

```text
- Derived only
- Never written as authority
- Never used for identity or uniqueness
- Never used in write paths
- MAY be used as a read-only query interface

All chronology-based lookups must resolve via structural traversal
(parent_event_id + sequence_index), not direct column matching.
```

---

### 3. Write Model

```text
All writes must go through ensure pattern.
No direct inserts allowed.
```

---

